soda-storyboard contains a Python port of all 14 recipes from manga-blueprint-studio.
Upstream files: layout-recipes.mjs (recipe metadata, row weights, width biases,
hero placement and geometry); layout-solver.mjs (reference for candidate affinity
without rearranging reading order); layout-modifiers.mjs (reference only).
Local source snapshots: docs/tasks/refs/manga-blueprint-studio/.
Implementation: src/soda_storyboard/templates.py and recipes.json.

Changes: Chinese names/help, configurable gutters, LTR mirroring, explicit order,
importance-based candidate ranking, seven-panel extensions (except the horizontal
recipe), and deterministic geometry with mutation=0. Seed/mutation, technique
advice, locks, insets and bleed are not ported. Shared-seam skew geometry,
maximum-area inscribed rectangles, polygon validation and overlay metadata are
original Python implementations. No OpenKoma source code has been copied.
No kumiko AGPL code is included. Full upstream MIT license follows.

The Chinese knowledge notes in skill/skills/soda-storyboard/references/ are
concise adaptations and synthesis from the local MIT source documents:
docs/tasks/refs/manga-blueprint-studio/MANGA-KNOWLEDGE.md,
docs/tasks/refs/manga-blueprint-studio/MANGA-TECHNIQUES.md,
docs/tasks/refs/manga-blueprint-studio/PANEL-LAYOUT-GRAMMAR-2026-09-12.md,
docs/tasks/refs/manga-blueprint-studio/MANGA-EXPRESSION-CATALOG.md.
MOSS-specific notes summarize this repository's phase0/phase0b/phase0d research;
they are not guarantees of image-generation quality. The plugin package carries
the same NOTICE and upstream MIT text for distribution.

